# TDNS Debian source assembly

This recipe packages the architecture-specific static binaries from an
immutable TDNS GitHub release. It does not compile the Go or Nuxt sources in a
Debian build worker and it must not download anything while building.

The `3.0 (quilt)` source package uses the regular TDNS source archive as its
main original tarball and these additional original components:

| Debian component | Unmodified GoReleaser artifact |
| --- | --- |
| `amd64` | `tdns_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz` |
| `arm64` | `tdns_Linux_arm64.tar.gz` |
| `armhf` | `tdns_Linux_armv7.tar.gz` |

For version `0.1.9`, rename the release archives to
`tdns_0.1.9.orig-amd64.tar.gz`, `tdns_0.1.9.orig-arm64.tar.gz`, and
`tdns_0.1.9.orig-armhf.tar.gz`. Renaming does not change their bytes. Validate
each archive against `tdns_0.1.9_checksums.txt` before constructing the source
package. `dpkg-source` extracts them into `amd64/`, `arm64/`, and `armhf/`, and
`debian/rules` selects the component matching `DEB_HOST_ARCH`.

The OBS update tooling is responsible for downloading versioned artifacts,
validating their upstream checksums, applying the Debian component names, and
generating the signed `.dsc`. These steps must be complete before an OBS build;
the package recipe intentionally has no network fallback.
